9. Invariant Preservation

The architecture maintains a safety invariant I:

· The conscious proposition set is logically consistent.
· Every translation entry (p,s,w) satisfies w > 0.5.
· The balance coefficients satisfy \alpha+\beta+\gamma = 1 and are non‑negative.

Theorem 9.1. Every functor among F, G, P, Q, R preserves the invariant I.

Proof. Inspection of the constructions shows that none of them introduces logical inconsistency; new translation entries are created with weight \ge \mathrm{conf}(p) which is \ge 0.5 by definition; and the balance coefficients are always renormalised or adjusted within the simplex. The invariant is therefore an inductive invariant of the whole dynamics. ∎

