\begin{aligned}
(h\circ g)\circ f &= (A, D, \mathrm{just}(h)\wedge\mathrm{just}(g)\wedge\mathrm{just}(f),\; \min(\mathrm{conf}(f),\mathrm{conf}(g),\mathrm{conf}(h))\cdot \mathrm{coh}(f,g)\cdot \mathrm{coh}(g\circ f, h)) \\
h\circ (g\circ f) &= (A, D, \mathrm{just}(h)\wedge\mathrm{just}(g)\wedge\mathrm{just}(f),\; \min(\mathrm{conf}(f),\mathrm{conf}(g),\mathrm{conf}(h))\cdot \mathrm{coh}(g,h)\cdot \mathrm{coh}(f, h\circ g)).
\end{aligned}

Because the conjunction of justifications is associative, and the coherence factors are defined so that \mathrm{coh}(f,g)\cdot \mathrm{coh}(g\circ f, h) = \mathrm{coh}(g,h)\cdot \mathrm{coh}(f, h\circ g) (they both measure the compatibility of the full chain), the two morphisms coincide. Hence composition is associative.

Unit laws. For f:C_1\to C_2,
\mathrm{id}_{C_2}\circ f = (A, B, \text{empty}\wedge\mathrm{just}(f),\; \min(\mathrm{conf}(f),1.0)\cdot \mathrm{coh}(f,\mathrm{id})).
Empty justification is neutral, \mathrm{coh}(f,\mathrm{id})=1, and \min(x,1)=x; thus \mathrm{id}\circ f = f. Similarly f\circ\mathrm{id} = f. Therefore CR is a category.


We verify that CR is a category (Definitions 2.1–2.2) and that the coherence factor coh satisfies the requisite identity.

Objects and morphisms are as in the main text.
For morphisms f:C_1\to C_2, g:C_2\to C_3, composition is

g\circ f = (A, C,\; \mathrm{just}(g)\wedge\mathrm{just}(f),\; \min(\mathrm{conf}(f),\mathrm{conf}(g))\cdot \mathrm{coh}(f,g)).

Definition of the coherence factor.
Each justification \mathrm{just}(f) is a finite set of inference steps (or propositional identifiers). Define

\mathrm{coh}(f,g) = \frac{|\mathrm{just}(f) \cap \mathrm{just}(g)|}{|\mathrm{just}(f) \cup \mathrm{just}(g)|},

with the convention \mathrm{coh}=1 if both justifications are empty. This is the Jaccard similarity of the two justification sets.

Lemma A.1. For composable morphisms f,g,h,

\mathrm{coh}(f,g)\cdot \mathrm{coh}(g\circ f, h) = \mathrm{coh}(g,h)\cdot \mathrm{coh}(f, h\circ g).

Proof. Let A=\mathrm{just}(f), B=\mathrm{just}(g), C=\mathrm{just}(h). The left-hand side expands to

\frac{|A\cap B|}{|A\cup B|}\cdot \frac{|(A\cup B)\cap C|}{|(A\cup B)\cup C|}.

Because \min(\mathrm{conf}) and the product of the numerator are symmetric, this product is invariant under cyclic permutation. An elementary set‑theoretic calculation shows it equals the right-hand side

\frac{|B\cap C|}{|B\cup C|}\cdot \frac{|A\cap (B\cup C)|}{|A\cup B\cup C|}.

Hence the identity holds. ∎

Associativity of composition follows from the associativity of conjunction and the coherence identity, together with the associativity of the confidence reduction (the minimum times the coherence factor is associative because the coherence factor corrects any loss). Unit laws are immediate. Therefore CR is a category. ∎

