Appendix B. The Category SP is Enriched Over ([0,1],\times,1)

From Definition 2.4, morphisms carry a real number \mathrm{sim}_f\in[0,1]. The composition rule is

\mathrm{sim}_{g\circ f} = \mathrm{sim}_f \cdot \mathrm{sim}_g \cdot \mathrm{compat}(f,g),

with \mathrm{compat}(f,g)\in[0,1] and \mathrm{sim}_{\mathrm{id}} = 1. This satisfies the axioms of an enriched category:

· The unit law: \mathrm{sim}_{\mathrm{id}\circ f} = 1 \cdot \mathrm{sim}_f \cdot \mathrm{compat}(\mathrm{id},f) and by definition \mathrm{compat}=1 for identities, giving \mathrm{sim}_f.
· Associativity of the hom-objects in the monoidal category ([0,1],\times,1) follows from associativity of multiplication and the requirement that \mathrm{compat}(f,g)\cdot\mathrm{compat}(g\circ f, h) = \mathrm{compat}(g,h)\cdot\mathrm{compat}(f, h\circ g), which holds by construction.

Thus SP is a category enriched over commutative monoid.

