Appendix E. Proof of the Adjunction P \dashv Q (Theorem 4.2)

The proof is dual to that of F \dashv G, exchanging the roles of propositions and pattern vertices.

Unit \eta_S: S \to Q(P(S)): Lifting a subconscious state S to Mii via P interprets each node as a proposition, then taking the quotient Q returns a subconscious state where those propositions are re‑encoded as nodes identical to the original ones. This gives a natural embedding.

Counit \varepsilon_M: P(Q(M)) \to M: Quotienting M extracts a subconscious state Q(M), then lifting it yields a meta‑state P(Q(M)) with trivial conscious structure. The counit morphism maps this to M by identifying the trivial propositions with their counterparts in M and resetting the balance.

